IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa10-types`

-- coa10-supplementary.l4: Chapter 12, ss 463, 469 and 470 of the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom): the directors' liability
-- for false or misleading statements in reports and statements, accounts filed in euros, and banking partnerships.
-- Lines 6325-6342, 6446-6454 and 6455-6461 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the official
-- text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer): JUST TRUE = the text says the case is
-- within the rule; JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words (each such branch carries
-- `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<the words>"`); NOTHING = the text does not decide
-- (each such branch carries `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 463: liability for false or misleading statements in reports and statements
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:6326 | (1) The reports and statements to which this section applies are—
-- src:6327 | (za) the strategic report,
-- src:6328 | (a) the directors' report,
-- src:6329 | (b) the directors' remuneration report, and
-- src:6330 | (c) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:6331 | (d) any separate corporate governance statement.
@ref s 463(1) The reports and statements to which the section applies (src:6326-6331)
DECLARE `s 463 kind of report or statement` IS ONE OF
    `s 463 the strategic report`
    `s 463 the directors' report`
    `s 463 the directors' remuneration report`
    `s 463 a separate corporate governance statement`
    `s 463 another report or statement`

-- src:6326 | (1) The reports and statements to which this section applies are—
-- src:6327 | (za) the strategic report,
-- src:6328 | (a) the directors' report,
-- src:6329 | (b) the directors' remuneration report, and
-- src:6330 | (c) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:6331 | (d) any separate corporate governance statement.
@ref s 463(1) Does the section apply to the report or statement (src:6326-6331)
GIVEN document IS A `s 463 kind of report or statement`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 463(1) the section applies to the report or statement` MEANS
    CONSIDER document
    WHEN `s 463 another report or statement` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed, fork F13): "The reports and statements to which this section applies are—" lists four and does not say "only"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (2) and (3): the director is liable to compensate the company for loss resulting from an untrue or misleading statement or an
-- omission, "only if" he knew (or was reckless) or knew the omission to be dishonest concealment of a material fact.
-- src:6332 | (2) A director of a company is liable to compensate the company for any loss suffered by it as a result of—
-- src:6333 | (a) any untrue or misleading statement in a report or statement to which this section applies, or
-- src:6334 | (b) the omission from a report or statement to which this section applies of anything required to be included in it.
-- src:6335 | (3) He is so liable only if—
-- src:6336 | (a) he knew the statement to be untrue or misleading or was reckless as to whether it was untrue or misleading, or
-- src:6337 | (b) he knew the omission to be dishonest concealment of a material fact.
@ref s 463(2), (3) The director is liable to compensate the company, only if he knew or was reckless (src:6332-6337)
GIVEN `s 463(1) the section applies to the report or statement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company has suffered loss as a result of an untrue or misleading statement in the report or statement, or the omission from it of anything required to be included in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he knew the statement to be untrue or misleading or was reckless as to whether it was untrue or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he knew the omission to be dishonest concealment of a material fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 463(2) the director is liable to compensate the company for the loss` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 463(1) the section applies to the report or statement`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies to this report or statement is not known
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section applies only to the reports and statements subsection (1) lists
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF NOT `the company has suffered loss as a result of an untrue or misleading statement in the report or statement, or the omission from it of anything required to be included in it`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "liable to compensate the company for any loss suffered by it as a result of"
        ELSE IF `he knew the statement to be untrue or misleading or was reckless as to whether it was untrue or misleading` OR `he knew the omission to be dishonest concealment of a material fact`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, an "only if"): "He is so liable only if— (a) he knew the statement to be untrue or misleading or was reckless as to whether it was untrue or misleading, or (b) he knew the omission to be dishonest concealment of a material fact."

-- (4) and (5): no liability to anyone other than the company for reliance on the information; "liability" includes another person
-- being entitled against him to a civil remedy or to rescind or repudiate an agreement.
-- src:6339 | (5) The reference in subsection (4) to a person being subject to a liability includes a reference to another person being entitled as against him to be granted any civil remedy or to rescind or repudiate an agreement.
@ref s 463(5) "liability" includes a civil remedy or a right to rescind or repudiate an agreement (src:6339)
GIVEN `the claim is that another person is entitled as against him to be granted a civil remedy or to rescind or repudiate an agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 463(5) the claim is within the liability that subsection (4) removes` MEANS
    IF `the claim is that another person is entitled as against him to be granted a civil remedy or to rescind or repudiate an agreement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes a reference to another person being entitled as against him to be granted any civil remedy or to rescind or repudiate an agreement"

-- src:6338 | (4) No person shall be subject to any liability to a person other than the company resulting from reliance, by that person or another, on information in a report or statement to which this section applies.
@ref s 463(4) No liability to a person other than the company resulting from reliance on the information (src:6338)
GIVEN `s 463(1) the section applies to the report or statement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is a person other than the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability results from reliance, by the claimant or another, on information in the report or statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 463(4) a person is subject to liability to the claimant` MEANS
    IF `s 463(1) the section applies to the report or statement` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the claimant is a person other than the company` AND `the liability results from reliance, by the claimant or another, on information in the report or statement`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person shall be subject to any liability to a person other than the company resulting from reliance, by that person or another, on information in a report or statement to which this section applies."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is limited to liability to a person other than the company resulting from reliance on information in a report or statement to which the section applies

-- (6): the section does not affect liability for a civil penalty or a criminal offence.
DECLARE `s 463 kind of other liability` IS ONE OF
    `s 463 liability for a civil penalty`
    `s 463 liability for a criminal offence`
    `s 463 any other liability`

-- src:6340 | (6) This section does not affect—
-- src:6341 | (a) liability for a civil penalty, or
-- src:6342 | (b) liability for a criminal offence.
@ref s 463(6) The section does not affect liability for a civil penalty or a criminal offence (src:6340-6342)
GIVEN liability IS A `s 463 kind of other liability`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 463(6) the section affects the liability` MEANS
    CONSIDER liability
    WHEN `s 463 liability for a civil penalty` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not affect— (a) liability for a civil penalty"
    WHEN `s 463 liability for a criminal offence` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not affect— ... (b) liability for a criminal offence"
    WHEN `s 463 any other liability` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence names only liability for a civil penalty and for a criminal offence

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 469: preparation and filing of accounts in euros
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:6447 | (1) The amounts set out in the annual accounts of a company may also be shown in the same accounts translated into euros.
@ref s 469(1) The amounts in the annual accounts may also be shown translated into euros (src:6447)
GIVEN `the amounts are set out in the annual accounts of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 469(1) the amounts may also be shown in the same accounts translated into euros` MEANS
    IF `the amounts are set out in the annual accounts of a company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The amounts set out in the annual accounts of a company"

-- src:6448 | (2) When complying with section 441 (duty to file accounts and reports), the directors of a company may deliver to the registrar an additional copy of the company's annual accounts in which the amounts have been translated into euros.
@ref s 469(2) When complying with section 441 the directors may deliver an additional copy of the annual accounts translated into euros (src:6448)
GIVEN `the directors are complying with section 441 (duty to file accounts and reports)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 469(2) the directors may deliver to the registrar an additional copy of the annual accounts translated into euros` MEANS
    IF `the directors are complying with section 441 (duty to file accounts and reports)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "When complying with section 441 (duty to file accounts and reports)"

-- src:6449 | (3) In both cases—
-- src:6450 | (a) the amounts must have been translated at the exchange rate prevailing on the date to which the balance sheet is made up, and
-- src:6451 | (b) that rate must be disclosed in the notes to the accounts.
@ref s 469(3) The amounts must be translated at the rate on the date to which the balance sheet is made up, and the rate disclosed in the notes (src:6449-6451)
GIVEN `the amounts have been translated at the exchange rate prevailing on the date to which the balance sheet is made up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that rate is disclosed in the notes to the accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 469(3A) the Companies Act individual accounts are those of a company that qualifies as a micro-entity for the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 469(3) the translation meets the requirements of the section` MEANS
    IF `the amounts have been translated at the exchange rate prevailing on the date to which the balance sheet is made up`
       AND (`that rate is disclosed in the notes to the accounts` OR `s 469(3A) the Companies Act individual accounts are those of a company that qualifies as a micro-entity for the financial year`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (a bare "must" not done, decided at this site, ruling of 2026-11-05): "In both cases— (a) the amounts must have been translated at the exchange rate prevailing on the date to which the balance sheet is made up, and (b) that rate must be disclosed in the notes to the accounts."

-- src:6452 | (3A) Subsection (3)(b) does not apply to the Companies Act individual accounts of a company for a financial year in which the company qualifies as a micro-entity (see sections 384A and 384B).
@ref s 469(3A) Subsection (3)(b) does not apply to a micro-entity's Companies Act individual accounts (src:6452)
GIVEN `s 469(3A) the Companies Act individual accounts are those of a company that qualifies as a micro-entity for the financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 469(3A) subsection (3)(b) requires the rate to be disclosed in the notes` MEANS
    IF `s 469(3A) the Companies Act individual accounts are those of a company that qualifies as a micro-entity for the financial year`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (3)(b) does not apply to the Companies Act individual accounts of a company for a financial year in which the company qualifies as a micro-entity"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence speaks only of a micro-entity's Companies Act individual accounts

-- src:6453 | (4) For the purposes of sections 434 and 435 (requirements in connection with published accounts) any additional copy of the company's annual accounts delivered to the registrar under subsection (2) above shall be treated as statutory accounts of the company.
@ref s 469(4) The additional copy is treated as statutory accounts for the purposes of sections 434 and 435 (src:6453)
GIVEN `the copy is an additional copy of the company's annual accounts delivered to the registrar under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 469(4) the additional copy is treated as statutory accounts of the company` MEANS
    IF `the copy is an additional copy of the company's annual accounts delivered to the registrar under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any additional copy of the company's annual accounts delivered to the registrar under subsection (2) above"

-- src:6454 | In the case of such a copy, references in those sections to the auditor's report on the company's annual accounts shall be read as references to the auditor's report on the annual accounts of which it is a copy.
@ref s 469(4) References to the auditor's report are read as references to the report on the accounts of which it is a copy (src:6454)
GIVEN `the copy is an additional copy of the company's annual accounts delivered to the registrar under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 469(4) the references in sections 434 and 435 to the auditor's report are read as references to the report on the accounts of which the copy is a copy` MEANS
    IF `the copy is an additional copy of the company's annual accounts delivered to the registrar under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case of such a copy"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 470: power to apply provisions to banking partnerships
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 470(1) (the regulation-making power) and (4) (its parliamentary procedure) are machinery (inert, reason 2).

-- src:6457 | (2) A “banking partnership” means a partnership which has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (c. 8).
-- src:6458 | But a partnership is not a banking partnership if it has permission to accept deposits only for the purpose of carrying on another regulated activity in accordance with that permission.
@ref s 470(2) "banking partnership" (src:6457-6458)
GIVEN `the partnership has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the partnership has permission to accept deposits only for the purpose of carrying on another regulated activity in accordance with that permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 470(2) the partnership is a banking partnership` MEANS
    IF `the partnership has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` AND (NOT `the partnership has permission to accept deposits only for the purpose of carrying on another regulated activity in accordance with that permission`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A “banking partnership” means a partnership which has permission under Part 4A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000. But a partnership is not a banking partnership if it has permission to accept deposits only for the purpose of carrying on another regulated activity in accordance with that permission."

-- src:6459 | (3) Expressions used in this section that are also used in the provisions regulating activities under the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 have the same meaning here as they do in those provisions.
-- src:6460 | See section 22 of that Act, orders made under that section and Schedule 2 to that Act.
@ref s 470(3) Expressions also used in the provisions regulating activities under the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 have the same meaning (src:6459-6460)
GIVEN `the expression is also used in the provisions regulating activities under the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 470(3) the expression has the same meaning as in those provisions` MEANS
    IF `the expression is also used in the provisions regulating activities under the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Expressions used in this section that are also used in the provisions regulating activities under the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000"
